  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0]) if h > 0 else 0\n    \n    # Find the two non-zero cells\n    cells = []\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                cells.append((r, c, grid[r][c]))\n    \n    if len(cells) != 2:\n        return grid\n    \n    (r1, c1, v1), (r2, c2, v2) = cells\n    \n    # Create output grid initialized with zeros\n    output = [[0 for _ in range(w)] for _ in range(h)]\n    \n    # Determine stripe orientation\n    if c1 == c2:\n        # Same column: horizontal stripes\n        is_vertical = False\n    elif r1 == r2:\n        # Same row: vertical stripes\n        is_vertical = True\n    elif abs(r1 - r2) > abs(c1 - c2):\n        # Taller than wide: vertical stripes\n        is_vertical = True\n    else:\n        # Wider than tall or equal: horizontal stripes\n        is_vertical = False\n    \n    if is_vertical:\n        # Vertical stripes (column-based)\n        if c1 < c2:\n            left_c, left_v = c1, v1\n            right_c, right_v = c2, v2\n        else:\n            left_c, left_v = c2, v2\n            right_c, right_v = c1, v1\n        \n        diff = right_c - left_c\n        period = 2 * diff\n        \n        for r in range(h):\n            # Fill columns for first value\n            c = left_c\n            while c < w:\n                output[r][c] = left_v\n                c += period\n            # Fill columns for second value\n            c = right_c\n            while c < w:\n                output[r][c] = right_v\n                c += period\n    else:\n        # Horizontal stripes (row-based)\n        if r1 < r2:\n            top_r, top_v = r1, v1\n            bottom_r, bottom_v = r2, v2\n        else:\n            top_r, top_v = r2, v2\n            bottom_r, bottom_v = r1, v1\n        \n        diff = bottom_r - top_r\n        period = 2 * diff\n        \n        for c in range(w):\n            # Fill rows for first value\n            r = top_r\n            while r < h:\n                output[r][c] = top_v\n                r += period\n            # Fill rows for second value\n            r = bottom_r\n            while r < h:\n                output[r][c] = bottom_v\n                r += period\n    \n    return output\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0]) if h > 0 else 0\n    \n    # Find the two non-zero cells\n    cells = []\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                cells.append((r, c, grid[r][c]))\n    \n    if len(cells) != 2:\n        return grid\n    \n    (r1, c1, v1), (r2, c2, v2) = cells\n    \n    # Create output grid initialized with zeros\n    output = [[0 for _ in range(w)] for _ in range(h)]\n    \n    # Determine stripe orientation\n    if c1 == c2:\n        # Same column: horizontal stripes\n        is_vertical = False\n    elif r1 == r2:\n        # Same row: vertical stripes\n        is_vertical = True\n    elif abs(r1 - r2) > abs(c1 - c2):\n        # Taller than wide: vertical stripes\n        is_vertical = True\n    else:\n        # Wider than tall or equal: horizontal stripes\n        is_vertical = False\n    \n    if is_vertical:\n        # Vertical stripes (column-based)\n        if c1 < c2:\n            left_c, left_v = c1, v1\n            right_c, right_v = c2, v2\n        else:\n            left_c, left_v = c2, v2\n            right_c, right_v = c1, v1\n        \n        diff = right_c - left_c\n        period = 2 * diff\n        \n        for r in range(h):\n            # Fill columns for first value\n            c = left_c\n            while c < w:\n                output[r][c] = left_v\n                c += period\n            # Fill columns for second value\n            c = right_c\n            while c < w:\n                output[r][c] = right_v\n                c += period\n    else:\n        # Horizontal stripes (row-based)\n        if r1 < r2:\n            top_r, top_v = r1, v1\n            bottom_r, bottom_v = r2, v2\n        else:\n            top_r, top_v = r2, v2\n            bottom_r, bottom_v = r1, v1\n        \n        diff = bottom_r - top_r\n        period = 2 * diff\n        \n        for c in range(w):\n            # Fill rows for first value\n            r = top_r\n            while r < h:\n                output[r][c] = top_v\n                r += period\n            # Fill rows for second value\n            r = bottom_r\n            while r < h:\n                output[r][c] = bottom_v\n                r += period\n    \n    return output",
